\begin{example}\label{ex-running-2}
The program $\prog_{y \geq 1}$ from \autoref{ex-running-1} is a
conjunctive linear lasso program.  Its normal form is
\begin{align*}
\stemt(q, y) \equiv\; &y \leq 1 \;\land\; -y \leq -1, \\
\loopt(q, y, q', y') \equiv\; &-q \leq 0 \;\land\; q' - q + y \leq 0
  \;\land\; -q' + q - y \leq 0 \\
  &\;\land\; y' - y - 1 \leq 0 \;\land\; -y' + y + 1 \leq 0.
\end{align*}
\end{example}


